[{"text":"Eps[a, b, c, d] is the head of the totally antisymmetric \\(\\epsilon\\) (Levi-Civita) tensor. The a,b, ... may have head LorentzIndex or Momentum.","anchor":"eps"},{"text":"When some indices of a Levi-Civita-tensor are contracted with 4-vectors, FeynCalc suppresses explicit dummy indices by putting those vectors into the corresponding index slots. For example, \\varepsilon^{p_1 p_2 p_3 p_4} (accessible via LC[][p1,p2,p3,p4]) correspond to \\varepsilon_{\\mu \\nu \\rho \\sigma} p_1^\\mu p_2^\\nu p_3^\\rho p_4^\\sigma.","anchor":"eps"},{"text":"Overview, EpsContract, EpsEvaluate, LC, LCD.","anchor":"see-also","section":"See also"},{"text":"Eps[LorentzIndex[\\[Mu]], LorentzIndex[\\[Nu]], LorentzIndex[\\[Rho]], LorentzIndex[\\[Sigma]]]","anchor":"cb1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\bar{\\epsilon }^{\\mu \\nu \\rho \\sigma }\\]","anchor":"cb1-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"Eps[Momentum[p], LorentzIndex[\\[Nu]], LorentzIndex[\\[Rho]], LorentzIndex[\\[Sigma]]]","anchor":"cb2","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\bar{\\epsilon }^{\\overline{p}\\nu \\rho \\sigma }\\]","anchor":"cb2-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"Eps[b, a, c, d] // StandardForm (*Eps[b, a, c, d]*)","anchor":"cb3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"Eps[ExplicitLorentzIndex[0], ExplicitLorentzIndex[1], ExplicitLorentzIndex[2], ExplicitLorentzIndex[3]]","anchor":"cb4","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\bar{\\epsilon }^{0123}\\]","anchor":"cb4-2","section":"Examples"},{"text":"Eps[LorentzIndex[\\[Mu]], LorentzIndex[\\[Nu]], LorentzIndex[\\[Rho]], LorentzIndex[\\[Sigma]]] * Pair[LorentzIndex[\\[Mu]], Momentum[Subscript[p, 1]]] Pair[LorentzIndex[\\[Nu]], Momentum[Subscript[p, 2]]]* Pair[LorentzIndex[\\[Rho]], Momentum[Subscript[p, 3]]] Pair[LorentzIndex[\\[Sigma]], Momentum[Subscript[p, 4]]] Contract[%]","anchor":"cb5","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\overline{p}_1{}^{\\mu } \\overline{p}_2{}^{\\nu } \\overline{p}_3{}^{\\rho } \\overline{p}_4{}^{\\sigma } \\bar{\\epsilon }^{\\mu \\nu \\rho \\sigma }\\]","anchor":"cb5-5","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\bar{\\epsilon }^{\\overline{p}_1\\overline{p}_2\\overline{p}_3\\overline{p}_4}\\]","anchor":"cb5-5","section":"Examples"},{"text":"Eps[LorentzIndex[\\[Mu]], LorentzIndex[\\[Nu]], LorentzIndex[\\[Rho]], LorentzIndex[\\[Sigma]]] Contract[% %]","anchor":"cb6","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\bar{\\epsilon }^{\\mu \\nu \\rho \\sigma }\\]","anchor":"cb6-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[-24\\]","anchor":"cb6-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"Eps[LorentzIndex[\\[Mu], D], LorentzIndex[\\[Nu], D], LorentzIndex[\\[Rho], D], LorentzIndex[\\[Sigma], D]] Contract[% %] // Factor2","anchor":"cb7","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\overset{\\text{}}{\\epsilon }^{\\mu \\nu \\rho \\sigma }\\]","anchor":"cb7-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[(1-D) (2-D) (3-D) D\\]","anchor":"cb7-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"ex1 = -(I/24) LCD[\\[Mu], \\[Nu], \\[Rho], \\[Alpha]] . GAD[\\[Mu], \\[Nu], \\[Rho], \\[Alpha]] // FCI","anchor":"cb8","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[-\\frac{1}{24} i \\overset{\\text{}}{\\epsilon }^{\\mu \\nu \\rho \\alpha }.\\gamma ^{\\mu }.\\gamma ^{\\nu }.\\gamma ^{\\rho }.\\gamma ^{\\alpha }\\]","anchor":"cb8-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"ex2 = -(I/24) LCD[\\[Mu]', \\[Nu]', \\[Rho]', \\[Alpha]'] . GAD[\\[Mu]', \\[Nu]', \\[Rho]', \\[Alpha]'] // FCI","anchor":"cb9","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[-\\frac{1}{24} i \\overset{\\text{}}{\\epsilon }^{\\mu '\\nu '\\rho '\\alpha '}.\\gamma ^{\\mu '}.\\gamma ^{\\nu '}.\\gamma ^{\\rho '}.\\gamma ^{\\alpha '}\\]","anchor":"cb9-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"DiracSimplify[ex1 . ex2] // Factor2 % /. D -> 4","anchor":"cb10","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[-\\frac{1}{24} (1-D) (2-D) (3-D) D\\]","anchor":"cb10-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[1\\]","anchor":"cb10-3","section":"Examples"}]